sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Customer as Customer<br/>PWA
  participant BFF as BFF<br/>API Gateway
  participant Order as Order<br/>session and cart owner
  participant Catalog as Catalog<br/>Table + Menu
  participant Redis as Redis<br/>operational state
  participant ODB as PostgreSQL<br/>Order DB

  Customer->>BFF: Open table QR link
  BFF->>BFF: Validate QR and session context
  BFF->>Order: Join or create table session
  Order->>Catalog: Validate QR token and table
  Catalog-->>Order: Table snapshot and current status

  alt Table is OCCUPIED with active session
    Order->>Redis: Read active session state
    alt Redis hit and not idle
      Redis-->>Order: Active session snapshot
      Order->>Redis: Refresh active session lifetime
      Order-->>BFF: Existing active session
    else Redis miss or stale
      Order->>ODB: Find active session by tenant/table
      Order->>Redis: Rebuild session snapshot
      Order-->>BFF: Rehydrated active session
    end
  else Table is AVAILABLE
    Order->>ODB: Create ACTIVE session row
    Order->>Redis: Create session snapshot
    Order->>Catalog: Mark table occupied for the session
    Catalog-->>Order: Updated table snapshot
    Order-->>BFF: New session
  else Idle empty session found
    Order->>ODB: Close only after durable empty-session checks
    Order->>Redis: Clear stale session/cart state
    Order->>Catalog: Mark table available
    Order->>ODB: Create replacement ACTIVE session
    Order->>Redis: Create replacement session snapshot
  end

  BFF-->>Customer: Return session context and menu entry data
  Customer->>BFF: Add or update shared cart item
  BFF->>Order: Mutate shared cart with expected version
  Order->>Catalog: Validate item is orderable
  Catalog-->>Order: Menu item snapshot, price, station
  Order->>Redis: Compare version and update cart atomically
  Order-->>BFF: Updated cart snapshot
  BFF-->>Customer: Updated shared cart

  Customer->>BFF: Submit order with idempotency key
  BFF->>Order: Submit order
  Order->>Redis: Read cart snapshot and validate version
  Order->>ODB: Lock session, create pending order and open bill
  Order->>Redis: Clear cart after version check
  Order-->>BFF: Order and bill snapshot
  BFF-->>Customer: Order submitted, waiting for staff confirmation

  Note over Order,Redis: Redis supports the hot path and Order DB remains the durable source for session and order decisions
